# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion programme's four-card window, WP6's own jobs (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fusion-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. WP6/ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is the placeholder for the tag the pack's B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env). The cards are
# under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# WS0 (EXACTNESS CONTROL): the audited lean twin of the W2 stack (c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-audit-lean: the draft-singles audit
# QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_SINGLES_AUDIT=all, the verify, vglue, draft-conv and draft-heads audits) with NONE of the WP6 levers. RECORD every answer's content hash, token count
# and finish reason from the smoke log: they are WS1's reference. READ: c2_smoke_check clean, no stall, no WP6 marker line at all (draft_wp6_smoke.py reports a leak).
# Duration (estimate): 50 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-audit-lean
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent8_code_32k
